ties between India and Bhutan. This initiative highlights Bhutan's commitment to boosting its Buddhist identity and serves as a token of gratitude for India's continuous support in its developmental journey.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/deeply-touched-pm-modi-thanks-bhutan-king-for-dedicating-sacred-stupa-in-his-honour/articleshow/135509436.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/deeply-touched-pm-modi-thanks-bhutan-king-for-dedicating-sacred-stupa-in-his-honour/articleshow/135509436.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-03T23:25:11+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aryan Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135509473,imgsize-99320.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[One move, two gains: NHAI to desilt Bihar rivers and build roads with excavated material]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/one-move-two-gains-nhai-to-desilt-bihar-rivers-and-build-roads-with-excavated-material/articleshow/135509375.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135509375.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Bihar's government has signed an agreement with the road transport ministry for river desilting to reduce flooding. The excavated silt and sand will be utilized in highway construction projects across the state. This initiative aims to improve water flow in rivers while providing construction materials at no cost. Bihar Chief Minister Samrat Choudhary emphasized the impact of flooding on the state's agriculture and infrastructure.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/one-move-two-gains-nhai-to-desilt-bihar-rivers-and-build-roads-with-excavated-material/articleshow/135509375.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/one-move-two-gains-nhai-to-de